* 一 4月 20 2026 Ferry Meng <mengferry@linux.alibaba.com> [5.10.134-19.4_rc1%%DIST%%]
- net/smc: fix NULL dereference and UAF in smc_tcp_syn_recv_sock() (Jiayuan Chen)
- net: fix refcount bug in sk_psock_get (2) (Hawkins Jiawei)
- PM: runtime: Fix a race condition related to device removal (Bart Van Assche) {CVE-2026-23452}
- nvdimm/bus: Fix potential use after free in asynchronous initialization (Ira Weiny) {CVE-2026-31399}
- netfilter: nf_conntrack_sip: fix Content-Length u32 truncation in sip_help_tcp() (Lukas Johannes Möller) {CVE-2026-23457}
- netfilter: nf_conntrack_h323: fix OOB read in decode_int() CONS case (Jenny Guanni Qu) {CVE-2026-23456}
- netfilter: nf_conntrack_h323: check for zero length in DecodeQ931() (Jenny Guanni Qu) {CVE-2026-23455}
- nfsd: fix heap overflow in NFSv4.0 LOCK replay cache (Jeff Layton) {CVE-2026-31402}
- wifi: wlcore: Fix a locking bug (Bart Van Assche) {CVE-2026-23420}
- net/sched: teql: Fix double-free in teql_master_xmit (Jamal Hadi Salim) {CVE-2026-23449}
- anolis: blk-throttle: pass bi_opf instead of bio_op() to preserve SYNC semantics (Joseph Qi)
- anolis: blk-throttle: fix io_start_time_ns not set for throttled bios (Joseph Qi)
- do_make_slave(): choose new master sanely (Al Viro)
- change_mnt_propagation(): do_make_slave() is a no-op unless IS_MNT_SHARED() (Al Viro)
- change_mnt_propagation() cleanups, step 1 (Al Viro)
- ext4: don't cache extent during splitting extent (Zhang Yi)
- anolis: writeback: fix race in insert_memcg_blkcg_link() (Ferry Meng)
- ext4: no need to verify new add extent block (yangerkun)
- anolis: ublk support legacy command opcode (Joseph Qi)
- ublk: prevent invalid access with DEBUG (Kevin Brodsky)
- Documentation: ublk: Drop Stefan Hajnoczi's message footnote (Bagas Sanjaya)
- ublk: Validate SQE128 flag before accessing the cmd (Govindarajulu Varadarajan)
- ublk: fix deadlock when reading partition table (Ming Lei)
- ublk: use vmalloc for ublk_device's __queues (Caleb Sander Mateos)
- ublk: sanity check add_dev input for underflow (Ronnie Sahlberg)
- ublk: santizize the arguments from userspace when adding a device (Ronnie Sahlberg)
- ublk: set_params: properly check if parameters can be applied (Uday Shankar)
- ublk: fix error code for unsupported command (Ming Lei)
- ublk: fix ublk_ch_mmap() for 64K page size (Ming Lei)
- ublk: don't allow user copy for unprivileged device (Ming Lei)
- ublk: move zone report data out of request pdu (Ming Lei)
- ublk: move ublk_cancel_dev() out of ub->mutex (Ming Lei)
- ublk: zoned: support REQ_OP_ZONE_RESET_ALL (Ming Lei)
- ublk: Switch to memdup_user_nul() helper (Ruan Jinjie)
- ublk: fix 'warn: variable dereferenced before check 'req'' from Smatch (Ming Lei)
- ublk: Fix signedness bug returning warning (Li Zetao)
- ublk: enable zoned storage support (Andreas Hindborg)
- ublk: move check for empty address field on command submission (Andreas Hindborg)
- ublk: add helper to check if device supports user copy (Andreas Hindborg)
- ublk: return -EINTR if breaking from waiting for existed users in DEL_DEV (Ming Lei)
- ublk: fail to recover device if queue setup is interrupted (Ming Lei)
- ublk: fail to start device if queue setup is interrupted (Ming Lei)
- ublk: make ublk_chr_class a static const structure (Ivan Orlov)
- ublk: add control command of UBLK_U_CMD_GET_FEATURES (Ming Lei)
- ublk: fix build warning on iov_iter_get_pages2 (Ming Lei)
- ublk: support user copy (Ming Lei)
- ublk: add read()/write() support for ublk char device (Ming Lei)
- ublk: support to copy any part of request pages (Ming Lei)
- ublk: grab request reference when the request is handled by userspace (Ming Lei)
- ublk: cleanup ublk_copy_user_pages (Ming Lei)
- ublk: cleanup io cmd code path by adding ublk_fill_io_cmd() (Ming Lei)
- anolis: Revert "task_work: allow TWA_SIGNAL without a rescheduling IPI" (Joseph Qi)
- ublk: kill queuing request by task_work_add (Ming Lei)
- ublk: fix AB-BA lockdep warning (Ming Lei)
- ublk: fix command op code check (Ming Lei)
- ublk: add timeout handler (Ming Lei)
- ublk: don't return 0 in case of any failure (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk: switch to ioctl command encoding (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk: make sure that block size is set correctly (Ming Lei)
- ublk: read any SQE values upfront (Jens Axboe)
- block: ublk_drv: cleanup 'struct ublk_map_data' (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk_drv: clean up several helpers (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk_drv: add two helpers to clean up map/unmap request (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk_drv: don't consider flush request in map/unmap io (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk_drv: add common exit handling (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk_drv: mark device as LIVE before adding disk (Ming Lei)
- ublk: remove check IO_URING_F_SQE128 in ublk_ch_uring_cmd (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk: improve handling device deletion (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: only allow owner to open unprivileged disk (Ming Lei)
- block: ublk: fix doc build warning (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: add mechanism for supporting unprivileged ublk device (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: add module parameter of ublks_max for limiting max allowed ublk dev (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: add device parameter UBLK_PARAM_TYPE_DEVT (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: move ublk_get_device_from_id into ublk_ctrl_uring_cmd (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: don't probe partitions if the ubq daemon isn't trusted (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: remove nr_aborted_queues from ublk_device (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: don't forward io commands in reserve order (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: add ublk_queue_cmd() for cleanup (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: avoid to touch io_uring cmd in blk_mq io path (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: comment on ublk_driver entry of Kconfig (Ming Lei)
- ublk_drv: support to complete io command via task_work_add (Ming Lei)
- task_work: allow TWA_SIGNAL without a rescheduling IPI (Jens Axboe)
- anolis: virtio-blk: add support for passing I/O flags to backend (Ferry Meng)
- anolis: nvme: add support for passing I/O flags to backend (Ferry Meng)
- virt: tdx-guest: Just leak decrypted memory on unrecoverable errors (Li RongQing)
- mm/slab: make __free(kfree) accept error pointers (Dan Carpenter)
- anolis: virt: tdx-guest: tsm api should be exclusive with ioctl (Zelin Deng)
- virt: tdx-guest: Add Quote generation support using TSM_REPORTS (Kuppuswamy Sathyanarayanan)
- mm/slab: Add __free() support for kvfree (Dan Williams)
- configfs-tsm: Introduce a shared ABI for attestation reports (Dan Williams)
- virt: coco: Add a coco/Makefile and coco/Kconfig (Dan Williams)
- locking: Introduce __cleanup() based infrastructure (Peter Zijlstra)
- dmaengine: ioat: Free up __cleanup() name (Peter Zijlstra)
- kbuild: Drop -Wdeclaration-after-statement (Peter Zijlstra)
- anolis: mm: clear I_KIDLED_YOUNG synchronously when shrink_slab (zhongjiang-ali)
- raw: fix a typo in raw_icmp_error() (Eric Dumazet)

